WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:03.598
How does each surviving pair become a rotating arrow?

00:00:03.878 --> 00:00:05.933
The weight and radius set its length.

00:00:06.213 --> 00:00:09.212
The difference of the indices sets how it turns.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.431
Each choice gives a power of z.

00:00:12.741 --> 00:00:15.286
Read p minus q from left to right.

00:00:15.596 --> 00:00:18.775
Three, one, minus one, minus three.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:22.277
Their weights are five sixteenths, three sixteenths,

00:00:22.417 --> 00:00:25.308
three sixteenths, and five sixteenths.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.613
Turn z again and watch the four arrows.

00:00:29.923 --> 00:00:32.461
For exponent k and weight w,

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:35.662
the length is w times rho to the power k.

00:00:35.972 --> 00:00:38.674
The angle is k times the angle of z,

00:00:38.814 --> 00:00:41.494
so a negative exponent reverses the turn.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:47.553
For example, z cubed has the radius cubed and three times the angle.

00:00:47.863 --> 00:00:50.821
Now place the four weighted arrows head to tail.

00:00:51.131 --> 00:00:55.789
The tip lands at the value of the third Legendre polynomial at our midpoint.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:04.060
In this product array, p plus q selects the Legendre degree, and p minus q selects the power of z.

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:11.214
At p equals three and q equals zero, five sixteenths times z cubed gives the blue arrow.

00:01:11.494 --> 00:01:17.880
At p equals two and q equals one, three sixteenths times z gives the mint arrow.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:24.994
At p equals one and q equals two, three sixteenths times z inverse gives the violet arrow.

00:01:25.274 --> 00:01:33.776
At p equals zero and q equals three, five sixteenths times z to the power minus three gives the orchid arrow.

00:01:34.056 --> 00:01:40.376
The gold arrow runs from the origin to the final tip and shows their sum, P three at J of z.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:44.650
What if we add one arrow for every Legendre degree?

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:49.700
The fourth is our whole four-arrow sum, multiplied by s cubed.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.500
Follow the tip in the zoom window as we add the first forty.

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:59.650
The gold diamond marks the limit. The smaller arrows keep closing the gap.

